Why generated IDs matter

One common reason to call SaveChanges() before the end is to get database-generated values.

Example:
var order = new Order();
context.Orders.Add(order);
Console.WriteLine(order.Id); // usually 0

await context.SaveChangesAsync();

Console.WriteLine(order.Id); // now database-generated ID

If later operations need order.Id, you may need a flush. However, if you are adding related entities through navigation properties, EF can often do it in one SaveChanges().

